<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2011/08/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata minClientVersion="2.12">
    <id>MimeKit</id>
    <version>5.0.0</version>
    <title>MimeKit</title>
    <authors>Jeffrey Stedfast</authors>
    <owners>Jeffrey Stedfast</owners>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://www.mimekit.net</projectUrl>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/jstedfast/MimeKit" />
    <icon>icons\mimekit-50.png</icon>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <description>
      MimeKit is an Open Source library for creating and parsing MIME, S/MIME and PGP messages on desktop and mobile platforms. It also supports parsing of Unix mbox files.

      As of v5.0, MimeKit is a meta-package that references both MimeKit.Core (MIME creation and parsing) and MimeKit.Cryptography (OpenPGP, S/MIME and DKIM/ARC support). This preserves backwards compatibility for consumers that expect cryptography support out of the box. If you do not need cryptography, reference MimeKit.Core directly instead.

      API documentation can be found on the web at http://www.mimekit.net/docs

      For those that need SMTP, POP3 or IMAP support, check out https://github.com/jstedfast/MailKit    </description>
    <summary>An Open Source library for creating and parsing MIME, S/MIME and PGP messages on desktop and mobile platforms.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
* Removed base, embed, input, link and source tags as "unsafe" tags. These are all void tags in HTML, meaning they do not have inner content. (issue #1247)
* Fixed InternetAddressListConverter to allow conversion of empty strings into an empty list. (issue #1249)
* Fixed NullReferenceException in BouncyCastleSecureMimeContext when SubjectKeyIdentifier is requested but not available. (issue #1250)
* Fixed MimeReader to support MimePart content larger than 2GB. (issue #1252)
* Fixed Message-Id parser to not decode international domains. (issue #1254)
* Bumped System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs dependency to 10.0.0.
* Bumped System.Text.Encoding.CodePages dependency to 10.0.0.
* Bumped BouncyCastle.Cryptography dependency to 2.7.0.

Note: As of BouncyCastle 2.7.0, decrypting S/MIME content encrypted with Blowfish, CAST5, RC2/40, RC2/64,
or RC2/128 will fail with a `CmsException: no fixed size for content-encryption key; constant-time RSA unwrap unavailable.`

Use the following code snippet to restore pre-2.7.0 behavior:

```csharp
Org.BouncyCastle.Utilities.Properties.SetThreadBoolean (Org.BouncyCastle.Utilities.Properties.CmsAllowLenientRsaPkcs1, true);
```
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>.NET Foundation and Contributors</copyright>
    <language>en-US</language>
    <tags>mime encryption arc dkim security smime s/mime openpgp pgp mbox mail email parser tnef</tags>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
